romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests annodu heluttade, server ge ondu rate limit ide mattu nimma request adannu daatide. Idakke kelegina karana galu irabahudu:

1. Ee request maduva code swalpa samayadalli tumbaa sala run agide, rate limit annu daatide.

2. Website, spam antha sandehisida request galannu 429 status code jote reject maduttade. Idara artha, user agent common browser alla antha irabahudu, idu kelavu website galu maduva simple check. Idannu sari madalu, neevu GET request ge "User-Agent" header annu ee reeti add madabahudu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

"browser.version" annu nijavada browser user agent string jote replace madabeku annodu gurutisabeku. Ee code run aguttiruva application annu avalambisi, idannu user agent spoofing antha pariganisabahudu, idu kelavu desha galu athava organization galu (athava code access madalu prayatnisuttiruva website na terms of service) kanoonu galalli nishedisabahudu.

3. Website bere yavudo karanakke request galannu rate limit maduttide. Idu request proxy moolaka madiddarinda agabahudu, aa sandarbhadalli proxy na bere users tumbaa request galannu madirabahudu, adare idu asadhyana.

4. Website denial of service attack ge olagagiruva karanakke ella request galannu reject maduttide. Idu asadhyana, yakeಂದರೆ aa reeti attack ge olagada server na sadharana behavior enendare traffic annu illada server ge route maduvudu, athava adannu sampoornavagi nishedisuvudu, yavude valid response annu kodade. Adare, website HTTP status code jote response madidaru kuda, adu server error 503 Service Unavailable agi irabahudu, server overloaded adaga idannu kodalagaduttade.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Yes, khandita! Neenu encounter madta iruva issue yake andre, "fizzbuzz", "fizz", mattu "buzz" annuva string literals temporary values. Neenu avugalige reference return madalu prayatnisutta idiya, adu allow illa. Yake andre avu scope mugida mele drop aaguttave, mattu return maadida reference dangling aagutte.

Ee error na fix madalu, neenu &str badalige &'static str return madabodu. &'static str andre string literals ge refer madutte, avugalige 'static lifetime irutte, andre avu program iruva varegu iruttave. Illi ninna code na updated version ide:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note madi, koneya arm Box::leak function na bagisikonddu String inda create maadida &'static str na return madutte. Idu Box<T> na ownership tegedukondu adara contents ge pointer na return madutte, effectivagii adanna leak madutte. Idu safe, yake andre return maadida pointer program iruva varegu irutte, aadare idanna care inda bagisabeku, yake andre idu automatically cleanup aagolla.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort ondu divide and conquer algorithm. Idanna input array na half aagi recursively split madutta hogutte, array single elements aago varegu. Adamele, sorted arrays na sorted order nalli matte merge madutte.

Bubble sort taraha simple algorithm ge compare madidre, merge sort na key benefits ivu:

1.  Idu ondu stable sort. Equal keys iruva elements na relative order na change madolla.
2.  Idu O(n log n) time complexity na efficiency na ide, idu dodda input sizes ge kooda relatively efficient algorithm agide. Bubble sort, innond kade, O(n^2) quadratic time complexity na ide, idu dodda inputs ge tumba inefficient agide.
3.  Idu ondu generic algorithm. Comparison function iruva yavude type data na sort madabahudu.

Illi ondu Rust implementation example ide:
```rust
